WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.917
Hello. In this tutorial you will install
ORIVEXY Verify on Odoo.sh, step by step,

2
00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:11.094
and leave it working with a
first test validation.

3
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:16.644
Before you pay, ORIVEXY Verify checks that every
IBAN in your payment batch belongs

4
00:00:16.644 --> 00:00:21.616
to who it says. It matches it against the
account ownership certificate your bank

5
00:00:21.616 --> 00:00:22.230
gives you.

6
00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:27.677
And it tells you which payments are correct,
which go to someone else and which

7
00:00:27.677 --> 00:00:32.925
accounts are not in the certificate. Everything
happens inside your Odoo, with your

8
00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:35.643
Odoo user: no bank data
leaves your server.

9
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:41.486
Before you start you need three things: an
Odoo.sh project with administrator

10
00:00:41.486 --> 00:00:47.379
rights, access to the project's GitHub
repository, and ORIVEXY Verify bought on Odoo

11
00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:50.747
Apps, for the same Odoo version
as your project.

12
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.895
Part two: preparation.

13
00:00:54.350 --> 00:01:01.645
Find ORIVEXY Verify on Odoo Apps and pick your
Odoo version, from 15 to 20. It costs

14
00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:08.419
€449.99, a one-time payment per version, with
no subscription. When you finish

15
00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:11.198
buying, you download a ZIP file.

16
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:16.991
Inside the ZIP is the orivexy_validator folder,
which is the module, all in one: the

17
00:01:16.991 --> 00:01:22.205
engine and its libraries are inside, so there
are no libraries and nothing else to

18
00:01:22.205 --> 00:01:22.714
install.

19
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:29.524
If you use Invoicing, orivexy_validator_account
connects to it and installs itself.

20
00:01:29.524 --> 00:01:35.592
The complete package for Odoo 18 also brings
the panel, tickets and the ORIVEXY

21
00:01:35.592 --> 00:01:36.206
colours.

22
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:43.599
Your Odoo.sh project keeps its modules in a
GitHub repository. If you don't have a

23
00:01:43.599 --> 00:01:47.666
project yet, go to odoo.sh and
press Create New.

24
00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:53.355
There you choose the repository, the Odoo
version and your Odoo Enterprise

25
00:01:53.355 --> 00:01:59.229
subscription code, and press Deploy. If you
already have a project, skip this step.

26
00:01:59.683 --> 00:02:04.988
Now, in a copy of the repository, create a
staging branch and copy the folders of

27
00:02:04.988 --> 00:02:08.131
the ZIP to the root, next to
your other modules.

28
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:15.107
Then git add, git commit and git push. That's
all. If you don't use the terminal,

29
00:02:15.107 --> 00:02:19.215
you can upload the folders from
the GitHub website.

30
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:22.410
Part three: installation.

31
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:29.463
In your Odoo.sh project, open the Branches tab:
the new branch shows up on its own.

32
00:02:29.463 --> 00:02:36.075
Drag it to Staging, and Odoo.sh will copy your
database and build the branch. There

33
00:02:36.075 --> 00:02:38.306
are no libraries to install.

34
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:45.445
When the build is green, press Connect. From
here on, what you see is real Odoo,

35
00:02:45.445 --> 00:02:48.542
version 18, with the ORIVEXY colours.

36
00:02:48.983 --> 00:02:56.255
First, turn on developer mode. Open the
apps menu and go to Settings.

37
00:02:56.717 --> 00:03:01.445
Scroll to the bottom of the page and press
Activate the developer mode.

38
00:03:01.883 --> 00:03:08.894
Now go to Apps and press Update Apps List, so
Odoo finds the modules of the new

39
00:03:08.894 --> 00:03:09.515
branch.

40
00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.950
Type ORIVEXY in the search box.

41
00:03:13.417 --> 00:03:20.065
There is ORIVEXY Verify. Press Activate and
wait a moment while it installs.

42
00:03:20.517 --> 00:03:26.452
When it finishes, open the apps menu: the
Validator is there. With the complete

43
00:03:26.452 --> 00:03:31.485
package, so are ORIVEXY Verify and
Tickets, each as a separate app.

44
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.094
Part four: initial setup.

45
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:41.332
ORIVEXY Verify works as soon as it is installed;
you only decide who sees what. The

46
00:03:41.332 --> 00:03:46.974
Validator role sees and reviews the validations
of the whole company. Accountants

47
00:03:46.974 --> 00:03:49.134
and signers see only their own.

48
00:03:49.583 --> 00:03:55.768
To give a role, open ORIVEXY Verify, Users and
permissions, and open the person's

49
00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:56.303
record.

50
00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:02.610
Tick the Validator role and save. With only the
Odoo Apps module, the equivalent

51
00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.638
permission is called Manager and
is in Settings, Users.

52
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:13.190
Everyone signs in to Odoo as usual, with their
Odoo user: ORIVEXY has no accounts or

53
00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.571
sign-in of its own.

54
00:04:15.017 --> 00:04:19.628
There are no licences or keys to activate
either, and no integrations to set up,

55
00:04:19.628 --> 00:04:22.625
because it does not connect to
any external service.

56
00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:27.643
Part five: a test validation,
with fictitious data.

57
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:34.103
Open the Validator. The panel sums up your
activity and, with a traffic light, the

58
00:04:34.103 --> 00:04:39.315
results of the last thirty days. The first
time, everything is at zero.

59
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:45.693
Press Try with sample data. ORIVEXY instantly
validates a fictitious batch against a

60
00:04:45.693 --> 00:04:49.230
fictitious certificate that
comes with the module.

61
00:04:49.683 --> 00:04:55.894
At the top is the verdict: there are issues.
Nine payments: six correct, two in the

62
00:04:55.894 --> 00:05:01.881
name of another holder and one whose IBAN is
not in the certificate. Each colour

63
00:05:01.881 --> 00:05:03.003
opens its rows.

64
00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:09.474
Below, every row has a coloured badge, the
masked IBAN, both holders side by side

65
00:05:09.474 --> 00:05:15.498
and the reason for the result. Here, Martines
with an s is not Martínez with a z.

66
00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:22.534
With See discrepancies you keep only what needs
attention. Open the payment to Pedro

67
00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:23.318
Fernández.

68
00:05:23.783 --> 00:05:28.986
The IBAN is in the certificate, but it belongs
to María López Ruiz. That payment

69
00:05:28.986 --> 00:05:32.759
should not go out without confirming
it with the supplier.

70
00:05:33.217 --> 00:05:39.664
Press Start review. If you try to resolve it
without writing anything, it won't let

71
00:05:39.664 --> 00:05:41.761
you: the note is mandatory.

72
00:05:42.217 --> 00:05:48.719
Write what you checked and press Resolve. The
note is recorded with your name and

73
00:05:48.719 --> 00:05:49.441
the date.

74
00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:58.654
From the validation you can print the PDF
report, with masked IBANs, or export the

75
00:05:58.654 --> 00:06:00.713
results to CSV or Excel.

76
00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:06.965
With your own files, press New validation:
upload one or more certificates, upload

77
00:06:06.965 --> 00:06:09.022
the batch and press VALIDATE.

78
00:06:09.483 --> 00:06:15.527
Any file finishes the validation. What cannot
be read, such as an image or a scan

79
00:06:15.527 --> 00:06:21.198
without text recognition, is left in manual
review with the reason, never as

80
00:06:21.198 --> 00:06:21.795
correct.

81
00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.765
And batches of more than two thousand rows are
validated in the background, in

82
00:06:26.765 --> 00:06:30.122
blocks, with a progress bar and a
notice when they finish.

83
00:06:30.583 --> 00:06:38.262
This is how to read the results. Correct:
nothing to do. Wrong holder: hold the

84
00:06:38.262 --> 00:06:44.191
payment and check it. Manual review:
you decide, with a note.

85
00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:51.357
IBAN not found: its certificate is missing.
And invalid IBAN: the number is

86
00:06:51.357 --> 00:06:52.162
mistyped.

87
00:06:52.617 --> 00:06:55.641
Part six: final check.

88
00:06:56.083 --> 00:07:01.041
The installation is complete if the Validator
is in the menu, if Try with sample

89
00:07:01.041 --> 00:07:06.124
data gives nine payments and six correct, and if
a user without the Validator role

90
00:07:06.124 --> 00:07:08.107
sees only their own validations.

91
00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:14.740
The most common errors are quick to fix. If
it is not in Apps, check that the

92
00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:21.333
folders are at the root of the branch and update
the list. If the build turns red,

93
00:07:21.333 --> 00:07:23.262
its logs say what fails.

94
00:07:23.717 --> 00:07:29.256
Always test in Staging. When everything is
right, merge the branch into production

95
00:07:29.256 --> 00:07:33.917
and, in that database, install the module
the same way you have seen.

96
00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:40.294
To update to a new version, replace the folders
with those of the new ZIP, push the

97
00:07:40.294 --> 00:07:43.158
change and upgrade the module from Apps.

98
00:07:43.617 --> 00:07:50.710
And that's it: ORIVEXY Verify installed and
working on Odoo.sh. If you need help,

99
00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:56.577
write to us from the module page on Odoo
Apps. Thanks for watching.
